syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "spirv_simplify", "description": "cheaper forms of a SPIR-V module's integer instructions, each proved by SAT; float instructions too (bit-exact, within Vulkan precision, or approximations).  code is SPIR-V assembly or GLSL (with spirv-cross installed, the result's glsl_view diffs its GLSL before and after); C code goes to the C frontend, as the c_optimize tool", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"code": {"type": "string", "description": "SPIR-V assembly, GLSL, or C (run as c_optimize)"}, "lang": {"enum": ["spv", "glsl", "c"], "description": "the code's language (by default from the code; c: the C frontend, as c_optimize)"}, "budget": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "seconds (6)"}, "ranges": {"type": "object", "description": "{\"n\": [lo, hi]}: values assumed for an input"}, "nofile": {"type": "boolean", "description": "a checksum instead of the rewritten module"}, "float_only": {"type": "boolean", "description": "only the float instructions"}, "exact": {"type": "boolean", "description": "float rewrites: bit-exact ones only"}, "ulp": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "float rewrites: within N ulp of the reference"}, "approx": {"type": "boolean", "description": "float rewrites: approximations too (with ulp)"}, "percomp": {"type": "boolean", "description": "float rewrites: per vector component"}, "search": {"enum": ["anneal", "cmaes"], "description": "float rewrites: the polynomials' coefficient search after rounding, kept when its certificate is better"}, "seed": {"type": "integer", "description": "the search's seed (UCAS_SEED, else 1)"}, "advice": {"type": "boolean", "description": "also report what could leave the shader: values of a draw's frequency, and in a fragment shader what is affine in the varyings"}, "overdraw": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "advice: the fragments a pixel gets (1 or more): the shader's runs that early fragment tests and a depth prepass save"}, "sink": {"type": "string", "description": "float rewrites: the format the stored and returned floats end in (unorm8, rgba8, r8g8b8a8_unorm, rgb10a2, f16): one step of it is the error budget; or int: a floor or an int() conversion may move its integer by one"}, "texture": {"type": "string", "description": "\"S B\": the descriptor set and binding the host gives a constant table's texture; a read of it is then written through the texture unit (without it, proposed)"}, "functions": {"type": "boolean", "description": "GLSL: the function-level pass alone (true) or not at all (false); both levels run by default"}, "float_ranges": {"type": "object", "description": "{\"c\": [lo, hi]}: a float input's range (closed)"}, "model": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name", "description": "the cost model to price and choose under (made the active one; the dot products it offers are used)"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["code"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"name": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"}, "number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "c_optimize", "description": "C99 in, faster C out for an x86-64 target: each rewrite proved (exhaustively, by SAT, by a derivation or by induction) against the original under C99 LP64 semantics with IEEE floats, unproved ones not applied; loops in closed form, element-wise loop bodies, strlen scans, loops vectorised with intrinsics (proved lane by lane)", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"code": {"type": "string", "description": "C99 source (or file)"}, "file": {"type": "string", "description": "a .c file instead of code"}, "target": {"type": "string", "description": "x86-64-v3 (default), zen4, skylake, alderlake, x86-64-v2 ... (c_targets)"}, "budget": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "seconds for proofs (10)"}, "range": {"type": "string", "description": "NAME LO HI: a contract on an input (\"x 0 1000\")"}, "check": {"type": "boolean", "description": "compile both with the host cc and compare them on edge and random inputs (UB inputs skipped)"}, "bench": {"type": "boolean", "description": "check, and time both with rdtsc"}, "wrapv": {"type": "boolean", "description": "signed overflow wraps (do not exploit UB)"}, "nofile": {"type": "boolean", "description": "print the code instead of a file"}, "timed": {"type": "boolean", "description": "say how many seconds the proofs took"}, "trace": {"type": "boolean", "description": "list every candidate and why it was not taken"}, "vecstub": {"type": "boolean", "description": "a stub vectoriser that rebuilds each counted loop from its IR (tests the loop extraction)"}, "vectorize": {"type": "boolean", "description": "apply the proved vectorised loops (by default they are proposed; with bench, applied where they beat clang's own code)"}, "engines": {"type": "string", "description": "which of ucas's engines generate candidates: all (default), none, or a comma list of find gates alg ring dio gf2 loops bound synth"}, "steps": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "sketches the synthesis may try per value (a deterministic budget; default 1000)"}, "ebudget": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "CPU 