a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "bockstein", "description": "the Bockstein spectral sequence: pages E_r, D_r and d_r of the exact couple of 0 -> C -p-> C -> C (x) Z/p -> 0, derived exactly until stable", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"space": {"type": "string", "description": "a space: S^n, T^n, RP^n, CP^n, K (Klein bottle), L(m) or L(m,q), pt; _s for a simplicial model (RP^2_s, T^2_s, K_s, S^3_s); X x Y, X v Y, susp(X); cells([[d1]], [[d2]], ...) by boundary matrices, facets([[0,1,2], ...])"}, "unreduced": {"type": "boolean", "description": "use the space's own cells (by default unit pivots are cancelled first, with the homotopy equivalence checked)"}, "p": {"type": "integer", "description": "a prime"}, "pages": {"type": "integer", "description": "at most this many pages (64)"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["space", "p"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "bockstein_trace", "description": "trace a in H^n(X; Z) through the Bockstein spectral sequence: j_r(p^(r-1) a) in E_r, in ker d_r?, in im d_r? (with a preimage)", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"space": {"type": "string", "description": "a space: S^n, T^n, RP^n, CP^n, K (Klein bottle), L(m) or L(m,q), pt; _s for a simplicial model (RP^2_s, T^2_s, K_s, S^3_s); X x Y, X v Y, susp(X); cells([[d1]], [[d2]], ...) by boundary matrices, facets([[0,1,2], ...])"}, "unreduced": {"type": "boolean", "description": "use the space's own cells (by default unit pivots are cancelled first, with the homotopy equivalence checked)"}, "p": {"type": "integer", "description": "a prime"}, "degree": {"type": "integer", "description": "n"}, "element": {"type": "string", "description": "[c1, c2, ...]: canonical coordinates in H^n(X; Z) (default: each generator)"}, "page": {"type": "integer", "description": "only page r"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["space", "p", "degree"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "prop01", "description": "check Proposition 0.1 of bockstein.pdf on a space: for a generating a Z summand of H^n(X; Z), j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r and not in im d_r, for every n and every r (all r up to the stable page, which covers the rest)", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"space": {"type": "string", "description": "a space: S^n, T^n, RP^n, CP^n, K (Klein bottle), L(m) or L(m,q), pt; _s for a simplicial model (RP^2_s, T^2_s, K_s, S^3_s); X x Y, X v Y, susp(X); cells([[d1]], [[d2]], ...) by boundary matrices, facets([[0,1,2], ...])"}, "unreduced": {"type": "boolean", "description": "use the space's own cells (by default unit pivots are cancelled first, with the homotopy equivalence checked)"}, "p": {"type": "integer", "description": "a prime"}, "pages": {"type": "integer", "description": "at most this many pages (64)"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["space", "p"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "theorem", "description": "state a theorem in the kernel's language (forall x:el, n:int: ..., and or not -> <->, = <= <, in; the library's sorts, functions and predicates: see lemmas and axioms)", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name", "description": "its name"}, "statement": {"type": "string", "description": "the formula"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["name", "statement"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"name": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"}, "number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "prove", "description": "prove a stated theorem: by the library's proofs of the same statement (every route, each re-checked independently), else by replaying the library's proofs and by automation; when it fails, a counterexample is searched in concrete Bockstein spectral sequences", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name", "description": "the theorem"}, "using": {"type": "array", "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name"}, "description": "lemmas and axioms for the automation"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["name"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"name": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"}, "number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "proof", "description": "print a proved theorem's proof: each route's script, the tree of lemmas it rests on with their kernel inferences, and the axioms used", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name", "description": "the theorem or library lemma"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["name"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"name": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"}, "number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "proof_check", "description": "re-check a proved theorem with the independent checker (kcheck.c)", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name", "description": "the theorem or library lemma"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["name"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"name": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"}, "number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "axioms", "description": "the axioms of the proof library (definitions and the integer arithmetic of Z); with a name, the ones that theorem's proofs rest on", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"$ref": "#/$defs/name", "description": "a proved theorem"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"name": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"}, "number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "lemmas", "description": "the proof library's lemmas and theorems", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "elliptic", "description": "an elliptic curve over Q: by default the summary (invariants, minimal model, Tate's algorithm: Kodaira symbols, c_p, conductor; torsion; rank bounds by 2-isogeny descent; generators and heights; periods, root number, L-values, analytic rank, BSD quotient), or one operation", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"curve": {"type": "string", "description": "[a1, a2, a3, a4, a6], [a4, a6], or \"y^2 + x*y = x^3 - x + 1\""}, "op": {"enum": ["info", "points", "torsion", "rank", "local", "minimal", "analytic", "periods", "on", "height", "add", "mul", "order", "wp", "ap", "model", "integral"], "description": "what (default: the summary)"}, "args": {"type": "string", "description": "the op's arguments: a point \"(x, y)\" (on, height, order), two points (add), \"k (x, y)\" (mul), a height bound (points, rank), a bound on |x| (integral), a prime (ap), z as \"a+bi\" (wp), a model: short, montgomery, edwards, twisted_edwards, legendre"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["curve"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "diophantine", "description": "solve a Diophantine equation through an elliptic curve: a plane cubic (homogeneous in 3 variables, or affine in 2), a curve quadratic in one variable with a quartic discriminant, or z^2 = quartic(x, y); rational point, birational map to Weierstrass form (kept with its inverse), the group, combinations of generators mapped back, each solution substituted into the equation; with no solution, a proof where one is found (rank 0, or no rational point on the real component the conditions need)", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"equation": {"type": "string", "description": "\"a/(b+c) + b/(a+c) + c/(a+b) = 4\""}, "positive": {"type": "boolean", "description": "every variable > 0"}, "integer": {"type": "boolean", "description": "integer values (affine equations)"}, "nonzero": {"type": "boolean", "description": "every variable != 0"}, "count": {"type": "integer", "description": "solutions wanted (default 1)"}, "maxmult": {"type": "integer", "description": "largest |coefficient| of a generator (default 30 for rank 1)"}, "search": {"type": "integer", "description": "point search bound"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["equation"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}}, {"name": "weierstrass", "description": "the maps from a cubic or quartic curve to Weierstrass form, the minimal model and the group", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"equation": {"type": "string", "description": "\"x^3 + y^3 = 7*z^3\""}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"],